WEBVTT

00:04.730 --> 00:08.610
Please be sure to give the chief's regards to Director Korobase.

00:08.610 --> 00:09.780
Oh, yes ma'am.

00:19.960 --> 00:22.420
Huh? What is this?

00:22.710 --> 00:26.550
Are Nanakorobi Nene and
Nanakorobi Clarion among you?

00:26.550 --> 00:28.420
Y-Yes, here.

00:28.420 --> 00:30.300
Nanakorobi Clarin?

00:30.640 --> 00:32.300
Step forward, slowly!

00:36.060 --> 00:37.640
The rest of you, stay put!

00:39.520 --> 00:40.560
U-Um...

00:41.310 --> 00:43.650
Confirmed. Hostages secured.

00:43.650 --> 00:44.320
Subdue them!

00:46.320 --> 00:47.570
Hostages?

00:47.570 --> 00:49.070
You two are safe now.

00:49.070 --> 00:52.320
You can thank a certain Uzal Delilah
for tipping us off as quickly as she did.

00:52.620 --> 00:53.830
Uzal did that?

00:54.700 --> 00:56.330
Where is she, might I ask?

00:56.330 --> 00:58.080
She was with us until we got on the elevator.

00:58.450 --> 00:59.620
What!?

00:59.620 --> 01:01.670
Put together a subterranean search team!

01:01.670 --> 01:02.380
Yes, sir!

01:07.670 --> 01:10.340
As technology advanced in nations around the world,

01:10.340 --> 01:13.760
cyborgs and autonomous robots
became more common in everyday life.

01:13.760 --> 01:17.720
During this era, the world was plagued with misfortune and conflict,

01:18.270 --> 01:21.730
and people wandered
far and wide in search of relief.

01:21.730 --> 01:25.980
This story has absolutely nothing to do with that era.

01:25.980 --> 01:28.990
This is a story of girl meets girl.

03:02.040 --> 03:04.790
Cenancle Island is
the perfect resort getaway!

03:04.790 --> 03:07.380
It's the island closest to heaven,

03:07.380 --> 03:10.210
where world-leading corporations coexist with a tropical paradise.

03:10.210 --> 03:12.420
And it's here that I, Vli—

03:11.300 --> 03:12.420
3, 2, 1!

03:14.380 --> 03:15.800
<i>I'm back!</i>

03:15.800 --> 03:16.680
She's resuscitated!

03:20.640 --> 03:23.810
<i>The last thing I remember is falling,
but here I am on the surface again.</i>

03:24.310 --> 03:25.770
<i>Way to go, me!</i>

03:25.770 --> 03:28.520
<i>"Today's report is on the idol who's been to hell and back, Vli..."</i>

03:29.360 --> 03:30.570
Wowie!

03:31.770 --> 03:34.190
Her house is so huge!

03:34.650 --> 03:36.610
And so is the door!

03:37.990 --> 03:40.450
Hello, is this Aunt Korobase?

03:41.080 --> 03:43.200
Yes! I'm right outside.

04:06.600 --> 04:08.560
Oh, sterilization. I see.

04:08.560 --> 04:10.400
We were a little dirty anyway.

04:10.400 --> 04:14.230
Huh? There's a plug for security registration?

04:15.070 --> 04:16.190
This must be it.

04:20.160 --> 04:21.910
Need some help, Clarin?

04:22.450 --> 04:23.660
I'll put it in you.

04:30.000 --> 04:31.750
Welcome, Nene!

04:31.750 --> 04:34.090
This is the first time we've met in person.

04:34.090 --> 04:36.010
I'm Korobase Takumi!

04:36.010 --> 04:37.050
In person?

04:37.050 --> 04:38.970
Today was a mighty sad disaster.

04:38.970 --> 04:41.260
Well, nice to meet you.

04:41.260 --> 04:43.050
Thank you for taking care of me so suddenly.

04:43.050 --> 04:46.770
Oh, don't sweat it. No need to be so polite.

04:47.230 --> 04:49.770
As of today, this is your house too.

04:49.770 --> 04:51.150
Kick back and relax.

04:51.150 --> 04:54.520
Uh, does that mean you're really my Aunt Taku—

04:54.520 --> 04:55.820
Stop with the "Aunt" nonsense!

04:55.820 --> 04:57.820
Just call me Takumi!

04:58.650 --> 05:00.570
Ta-ku-mi-chan!

05:00.570 --> 05:01.860
Y-Yes, ma'am!

05:02.370 --> 05:03.620
Well, never mind that.

05:03.620 --> 05:04.530
More importantly...

05:04.870 --> 05:07.500
Why is <i>that</i> thing in your possession!?

05:08.580 --> 05:10.790
Oh, I'm sorry. A lot happened...

05:11.170 --> 05:14.540
There's even a forged encrypted certificate
for its international AI registration.

05:15.750 --> 05:17.050
Message from Uzal.

05:17.960 --> 05:19.300
Give it here!

05:23.260 --> 05:24.930
Hi!

05:24.930 --> 05:27.010
Long time no see, Takumi!

05:27.010 --> 05:28.180
Oh, Uzal!

05:28.180 --> 05:32.190
Came into possession of a new toy
and thought you'd hog all the fun, eh?

05:32.190 --> 05:36.230
<i></i>But we all know how you treat your toys,
so I sent along Clarion to be your babysitter.

05:36.230 --> 05:39.530
I would never forgive you for ruining a toy as fun as Nene.

05:40.320 --> 05:41.740
Shut yer trap!

05:41.740 --> 05:43.070
I found her first!

05:43.070 --> 05:44.070
It's mine!

05:44.070 --> 05:44.950
You dummy!

05:44.950 --> 05:48.200
Do you know how hard it was to
snatch her away from that facility!?

05:49.410 --> 05:54.710
Oh, and P.S., I wrecked nearly all those Gertsecommas I got! Whoopsies! Sorry!

05:54.710 --> 05:55.840
You jerk!

05:58.050 --> 06:01.550
And you! How the heck do you know her in the first place!?

06:01.550 --> 06:02.840
We met on the ship.

06:02.550 --> 06:06.510
Girl

06:03.720 --> 06:06.510
meets

06:04.680 --> 06:06.510
girl!

06:06.510 --> 06:09.180
And then she started taking care of me.

06:11.180 --> 06:12.690
I've got a mad headache.

06:13.100 --> 06:15.650
Now I've gotta take care of you, too?

06:15.650 --> 06:18.980
But we got separated from Uzal along the way.

06:18.980 --> 06:20.190
I'm worried.

06:20.190 --> 06:22.820
She doesn't deserve your concern.

06:22.820 --> 06:26.570
I bet she pushed the responsibility onto someone else and ran off.

06:26.570 --> 06:28.700
You two seem close.

06:28.700 --> 06:30.330
Absolutely not!

06:30.330 --> 06:32.790
Well, first come, first served, in the end.

06:32.790 --> 06:35.210
From now on, <i>this</i> is your home.

06:35.210 --> 06:37.960
Once again, welcome, Nene.

06:40.460 --> 06:41.460
Thank you.

06:42.050 --> 06:44.590
By the way, where is your luggage?

06:46.340 --> 06:48.100
I lost it.

06:48.100 --> 06:50.720
Then we'll go shopping tomorrow.

06:50.720 --> 06:53.600
Today's probably got you beat,
so go get some rest.

06:53.890 --> 06:54.640
Yes, ma'am!

06:55.850 --> 06:57.480
There's no point in changing clothes.

06:57.810 --> 06:59.770
You wear pajamas to bed.

06:59.770 --> 07:00.860
Now <i>and</i> in real life.

07:02.320 --> 07:03.860
Clarin, you're so cute!

07:10.580 --> 07:11.740
What's so amusing?

07:13.410 --> 07:17.250
I just realized I'll get to be with you every day from now on!

07:22.250 --> 07:23.760
Such nice weather!

07:24.050 --> 07:25.880
Going outside is the best!

07:25.880 --> 07:28.180
Hurry up! This way!

07:28.640 --> 07:32.260
If you're going shopping on Cenancle Island,
you want Area Mercury!

07:32.260 --> 07:35.850
You can buy anything your heart
desires here, if you've got the money!

07:35.850 --> 07:37.400
That's usually how malls work.

07:37.690 --> 07:40.610
What will we buy today, I wonder.

07:40.610 --> 07:42.650
Hey, how are you feeling?

07:42.650 --> 07:44.030
Are you not feeling well?

07:44.900 --> 07:48.360
Self-diagnostic composite value: 92 points.

07:48.360 --> 07:49.200
Healthy.

07:49.200 --> 07:50.160
Okay.

07:50.160 --> 07:54.790
I bet yesterday's craziness surprised you, but this island's usually peaceful.

07:54.790 --> 07:56.210
Rest assured.

07:56.210 --> 07:56.790
I see.

07:57.290 --> 07:58.540
Nene, get down!

07:58.540 --> 08:00.170
Warning: imminent attack.

08:00.170 --> 08:01.340
<i>Threat level: high.</i>

08:01.340 --> 08:03.550
C-Clarin... Your face is...

08:05.550 --> 08:08.050
<i>Threat to Nanakorobi Nene confirmed.</i>

08:08.380 --> 08:10.550
<i>Third-priority objective: owner protection.</i>

08:11.550 --> 08:12.810
Clarin, stop!

08:17.060 --> 08:19.190
Clarin, are you okay!?

08:21.650 --> 08:24.190
Sick 'em! You can do it!

08:25.320 --> 08:26.780
Aunt Ta—

08:27.360 --> 08:29.820
You've been cyberized too, Takumi.

08:29.820 --> 08:30.780
Yeah.

08:30.780 --> 08:36.200
But unlike you, everything but what's needed for my cyberbrain is flesh.

08:36.700 --> 08:40.710
Listening to the administration and human rights group argue about them gives me a headache,

08:40.710 --> 08:42.460
but I avoid getting into that junk.

08:42.460 --> 08:44.710
Don't you find cyberbrains handy, too?

08:44.710 --> 08:48.840
It was kind of a requirement to be a cyborg, so I'm not sure yet.

08:48.840 --> 08:50.550
It's a question of time, for sure.

08:50.550 --> 08:54.220
Someday this technology will transform the world.

08:54.560 --> 08:59.230
Sometimes I lose track of what's real, though.

09:01.980 --> 09:04.060
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

09:05.480 --> 09:06.730
Are you okay?

09:06.730 --> 09:07.740
I'll wipe that off.

09:08.490 --> 09:09.400
I know, I know.

09:09.400 --> 09:10.740
I won't touch your ears.

09:11.820 --> 09:14.160
You're Little Miss Careless today, aren't you?

09:15.410 --> 09:17.830
Something special about those ears?

09:26.670 --> 09:28.420
I've gotta know!

09:29.050 --> 09:30.720
Slow down!

09:30.420 --> 09:31.930
You shouldn't do that...

09:38.270 --> 09:40.230
You really shouldn't!

09:38.890 --> 09:41.600
That's Uzal's puppet for you.

09:41.600 --> 09:44.020
But how about this!?

09:45.480 --> 09:47.570
<i>Your mistress is in a fix.</i>

09:47.570 --> 09:48.860
<i>What will you do </i>now<i>?</i>

09:48.860 --> 09:51.860
Stop it! What are these things!?

09:52.490 --> 09:55.870
Whoa, the lasers didn't fool her for long.

09:55.870 --> 09:59.370
And she could tell it was my doing instantly.

10:01.830 --> 10:04.250
I hate to admit it, but you put on a good show.

10:04.250 --> 10:06.630
But you're still just a puppet. Too bad!

10:13.680 --> 10:15.470
Resistance is futile!

10:16.680 --> 10:17.890
Accept your fate.

10:17.890 --> 10:19.180
Um...

10:18.350 --> 10:21.100
This kind of stuff is so thrilling!

10:20.560 --> 10:22.980
She really hates what you're doing...

10:21.100 --> 10:22.140
Just a little...

10:22.140 --> 10:24.020
Just a little!

10:22.980 --> 10:24.020
I refuse! Absolutely refuse!

10:25.770 --> 10:27.020
No!

10:33.400 --> 10:34.610
Please stop!

10:35.990 --> 10:37.490
What are you doing?

10:41.040 --> 10:43.620
Pandora Device, open!

10:43.620 --> 10:44.750
Supplemental skill software!?

10:45.170 --> 10:48.880
Release skill, Elpis Series. Hacker!

10:53.420 --> 10:54.260
The barriers!

10:57.010 --> 10:59.010
Don't erase the data!

10:59.010 --> 11:01.720
I worked hard to tune this terrarium!

11:01.720 --> 11:03.850
Quit it!

11:03.850 --> 11:04.770
Oh, that's right!

11:04.770 --> 11:08.270
There was going to be a welcome parade
and fireworks in your honor, Nene!

11:33.170 --> 11:33.920
Bad girl!

11:34.380 --> 11:35.930
Don't pick on Clarin!

11:36.300 --> 11:39.930
Forcing someone to do
something they hate is wrong!

11:39.930 --> 11:41.510
<i>What the heck is she!?</i>

11:41.510 --> 11:43.430
<i>How did she get in here?</i>

11:43.430 --> 11:46.560
When did you realize that was a simulation?

11:46.560 --> 11:47.850
When?

11:48.480 --> 11:49.650
Wait a minute.

11:49.650 --> 11:51.110
Let me rephrase the question.

11:51.110 --> 11:54.740
What happened when you arrived at my house?

11:54.740 --> 11:56.530
Clarin and I were sterilized.

11:56.530 --> 11:59.030
We sat on the couch and plugged in...

11:59.030 --> 12:02.080
And then we played a game for a half hour,
where we all went on a walk.

12:02.330 --> 12:03.910
G-Game!?

12:03.910 --> 12:06.250
Then you knew the whole time?

12:06.250 --> 12:09.830
But even military AI could've been fooled by that terrarium!

12:12.420 --> 12:14.050
Games are my specialty.

12:14.050 --> 12:15.970
<i>She's a natural barrier-breaker.</i>

12:15.970 --> 12:18.220
<i>Nanakorobi Nene, an Adepter.</i>

12:18.550 --> 12:21.680
<i>She's even more interesting than I expected!</i>

12:21.680 --> 12:23.100
So once again...

12:23.680 --> 12:27.100
Nice to meet you, Takumi.

12:27.100 --> 12:29.020
I'm Nanakorobi Nene.

12:29.020 --> 12:30.690
Now we can shake hands for real.

12:33.070 --> 12:35.110
Uh, hello?

12:49.790 --> 12:53.590
The Cenancle Self-Governance Organization has announced

12:53.590 --> 12:57.840
that the damage around Vulcan Harbor was the result of bedrock collapse from a suicide bombing.

12:59.220 --> 13:05.100
The ringleader was the internationally wanted terrorist
Sahar Schehera, whose death has been confirmed.

13:05.600 --> 13:07.680
Furthermore, the Self-Governance Organization

13:07.680 --> 13:10.640
will claim damages in the amount of $30 billion,

13:10.640 --> 13:14.610
as well as impose criminal penalties on the accomplices now in custody.

13:14.900 --> 13:17.740
And today, a solemn funeral mass was held for Uzal Delilah,

13:18.030 --> 13:22.530
a representative of the Rhea Foundation
who died in the terrorist attack.

13:22.530 --> 13:23.620
It's Uzal.

13:24.410 --> 13:27.750
Ms. Delilah had made many contributions
to fields such as education and medical care.

13:27.750 --> 13:33.670
Many came to mourn her loss and place bouquets in her memory.

13:27.750 --> 13:33.670
Uzal would laugh if she came back and saw a funeral this grand all for her.

13:34.250 --> 13:39.340
I risked my life for this scoop, and they throw it in this worthless news report!?

13:39.340 --> 13:40.510
Those fools!

13:40.510 --> 13:42.800
So what? They paid good money for it.

13:42.800 --> 13:45.930
And the fees for your hospitalization
and destroyed equipment were no joke.

13:45.930 --> 13:48.520
Don't go thinking I'll give up just 'cause of that!

13:49.220 --> 13:53.440
The long famed terrorist group will soon be transferred here, the Sisyphus Correctional Facility.

13:53.440 --> 13:56.150
Whoa, for real!? They actually came!?

13:59.440 --> 14:03.740
This report is coming to you live by the reporter who went to hell and back, Vli—

14:04.410 --> 14:05.370
This is a follow-up report.

14:05.370 --> 14:08.910
An explosion from the terrorist group's
transport convoy has just been reported.

14:08.910 --> 14:10.000
Whew.

14:10.000 --> 14:12.500
I managed to restore from a backup.

14:19.550 --> 14:21.550
An intruder?

14:30.100 --> 14:31.810
Sleep well, Clarin?

14:31.810 --> 14:33.440
I don't sleep.

14:33.980 --> 14:35.940
Good morning, Takumi.

14:39.230 --> 14:40.900
U-Um...

14:47.200 --> 14:50.290
There are inconsistencies in 4,464 of the design files!

14:50.290 --> 14:51.250
Thirty—

14:51.870 --> 14:54.210
Oh, sorry. Here.

14:54.210 --> 14:56.960
That project's okay as number 204!

14:57.330 --> 14:59.210
She's busy working.

14:59.210 --> 15:01.460
Get dressed and wait in the next room!

15:04.470 --> 15:08.600
The weather's nice, so you two should <i>actually</i> go shopping today.

15:08.600 --> 15:13.020
I'll have a few Gertsecommas guide you, so check out the city while you're at it.

15:13.020 --> 15:13.600
Yes, ma'am.

15:14.020 --> 15:15.850
See you later!

15:16.190 --> 15:18.310
Is there anything you'd like, Clarin?

15:18.310 --> 15:20.020
Equipment and reserves.

15:20.020 --> 15:21.860
Okay, let's go buy some.

15:21.860 --> 15:23.610
So they're what she's after.

15:24.110 --> 15:27.570
But is Nene her target?

15:27.570 --> 15:29.620
Or perhaps Uzal's puppet?

15:31.120 --> 15:33.000
Oh yeah!

15:33.000 --> 15:36.370
Um, is it okay if I call you all Gercomas?

15:36.960 --> 15:40.960
Are you the same ones who helped us out underground?

15:40.960 --> 15:44.760
They're still under development,
so their software is being updated all the time.

15:44.760 --> 15:47.130
The ones Uzal had were a previous version.

15:48.260 --> 15:49.510
They're mainly the same.

15:49.510 --> 15:53.060
I see. You know a lot, Clarin.

15:53.060 --> 15:57.270
Thanks for helping Clarin that time, Gercoma.

15:57.270 --> 15:59.150
Good boy.

15:59.770 --> 16:02.940
But Gertsecommas don't even have feelings.

16:02.940 --> 16:04.780
What a weird girl.

16:22.090 --> 16:25.300
Nene, could you run an errand for me?

16:25.300 --> 16:26.920
Sure, no problem.

16:26.920 --> 16:28.970
I'll tell you where to go.

16:30.180 --> 16:32.930
Let's see. This must be Area Charon.

16:33.390 --> 16:36.600
Look at all the funny looking billboards, Clarin.

16:37.520 --> 16:43.690
Making her go through the red-light district at night would be wrong, but it's deserted during the day.

16:44.270 --> 16:47.190
I've given you an opening,
so show me your next move.

16:47.570 --> 16:49.150
Which one're you after, huh?

16:49.150 --> 16:51.530
I couldn't care less if you're after Uzal's puppet,

16:51.530 --> 16:56.330
but if it's Nene, I'll squash you and the entire organization you're working for.

17:05.840 --> 17:07.590
Go, follow them!

17:09.930 --> 17:11.090
I've had enough of this!

17:11.430 --> 17:14.100
What is it you're after!?

17:14.100 --> 17:15.850
These are Sahar's robots!

17:16.220 --> 17:17.720
So you know of <i>Sahar</i>!?

17:21.350 --> 17:22.190
Ow!

17:22.190 --> 17:23.900
Give it up!

17:23.900 --> 17:24.730
Don't touch there!

17:26.280 --> 17:28.110
You're younger than I expected.

17:28.110 --> 17:29.740
State your affiliation and objective!

17:29.740 --> 17:30.900
What's the big idea!?

17:30.900 --> 17:32.070
Stay out of my way!

17:32.070 --> 17:35.740
Everybody's counting on me to get BUER's authentication key!

17:36.490 --> 17:39.500
BUER!? Hey, did you just say BU—

17:39.830 --> 17:41.040
Viral intrusion!?

17:41.040 --> 17:42.420
Am I being hacked!?

17:42.420 --> 17:44.880
But only my connection
to the Gertsecommas!?

17:44.880 --> 17:48.170
Nobody ever gets past my barriers!

17:48.550 --> 17:49.880
Who the heck's doing this!?

17:57.010 --> 17:57.930
What do <i>you</i> want?

17:57.930 --> 17:59.930
Stalking someone is wrong!

17:59.930 --> 18:01.310
Deja vu...

18:01.310 --> 18:05.020
And Clarin wanted to keep that a secret.

18:05.020 --> 18:07.070
You're referring to BUER?

18:07.070 --> 18:08.150
Unfortunate, but acceptable.

18:08.150 --> 18:09.070
Hey, hold up!

18:09.070 --> 18:10.360
The hell's going on here!?

18:10.360 --> 18:11.820
Untie me!

18:14.740 --> 18:16.870
It's not like I was following you.

18:16.870 --> 18:17.950
I just happened to see you.

18:18.830 --> 18:20.200
Who are you, exactly?

18:20.200 --> 18:21.710
It's me! Me!

18:21.710 --> 18:23.370
Couldn't you tell!?

18:24.750 --> 18:26.340
If I saw the chance, I'd stea—

18:27.250 --> 18:28.460
I'd nego—

18:30.170 --> 18:31.590
Oh, screw it!

18:32.010 --> 18:33.880
It doesn't look like you have them on you,

18:33.880 --> 18:35.340
so have you seen Sahar's glasses?

18:35.640 --> 18:36.930
Glasses...

18:36.930 --> 18:38.390
Oh, you mean those?

18:38.390 --> 18:41.020
Right! BUER's <i>real</i> authentication key!

18:41.020 --> 18:43.980
Come to think of it, what <i>did</i> happen to them?

18:44.310 --> 18:46.060
Please figure it out for me!

18:46.060 --> 18:47.360
I need them by tomorrow!

18:47.360 --> 18:48.860
By tomorrow?

18:48.860 --> 18:50.110
Yes, by tomorrow!

18:51.110 --> 18:53.110
You have them after all!?

18:54.030 --> 18:54.860
What is it?

18:55.320 --> 18:56.280
You want me to beg!?

18:56.280 --> 18:58.700
I'll grovel at your feet!

18:59.530 --> 19:02.200
Wrong. I was given instructions.

19:02.200 --> 19:03.750
Instructions?

19:03.750 --> 19:06.750
Hey there, morons. You alive?

19:06.750 --> 19:07.960
Uzal.

19:07.960 --> 19:09.840
Well, knowing you girls,

19:09.840 --> 19:14.130
the mastermind probably caught you,
and you'll be killed if you talk.

19:14.130 --> 19:16.550
But I'm sure you're not <i>that</i> useless.

19:17.720 --> 19:20.470
But with all the generosity my bosom contains,

19:20.470 --> 19:22.850
I've left instructions for the key to be given to you.

19:22.850 --> 19:25.600
I'm tempted to make you shake your butt and make rabbit sounds...

19:25.600 --> 19:26.400
Hop!? Hop!?

19:26.400 --> 19:27.650
but you'd just look silly.

19:31.070 --> 19:32.570
Stupid idiot!

19:32.570 --> 19:33.940
Were <i>those</i> your last words?

19:33.940 --> 19:35.780
Well, don't expect any gratitude from me!

19:36.150 --> 19:38.030
Think of it as severance pay.

19:38.030 --> 19:39.780
Give my regards to the mastermind.

19:39.780 --> 19:42.290
You sure about this, Clarin?

19:42.290 --> 19:43.290
Nene.

19:43.580 --> 19:45.540
I would like to stop somewhere.

19:48.040 --> 19:49.630
I've got the key.

19:49.630 --> 19:50.750
Oh?

19:50.750 --> 19:52.550
This is BUER's authentication key.

19:52.960 --> 19:55.300
A storage key in the form of glasses, eh?

19:56.130 --> 20:00.220
I saved you from the police to keep information from leaking out,

20:00.220 --> 20:03.680
but I'm sure we're both aware of the <i>easiest</i> way to cover this up.

20:03.970 --> 20:06.100
Give me another chance!

20:06.100 --> 20:08.770
I know now how to activate BUER properly!

20:09.560 --> 20:11.940
And please... you promised.

20:11.940 --> 20:14.400
Have you considered

20:14.400 --> 20:18.950
how many hours of my precious time were wasted due to your group's failure?

20:20.410 --> 20:21.950
I apologize...

20:22.780 --> 20:25.330
This is where we came up to the surface.

20:25.700 --> 20:27.580
This is sooner than planned,

20:27.580 --> 20:32.840
but I was told I could reveal this
information once Korobase heard about BUER.

20:36.760 --> 20:39.180
Much time did I spend in contemplation.

20:39.180 --> 20:42.100
Time enough to identify the truth.

20:42.430 --> 20:45.470
Vile brutes! I was incarcerated much too long!

20:45.470 --> 20:47.770
I do detest dark places!

20:47.770 --> 20:51.060
I had planned to leave you buried for months.

20:51.060 --> 20:53.190
I am experiencing fear...

20:53.190 --> 20:55.030
Sorry we forgot about you.

20:55.030 --> 20:56.860
Thy bluntness makes thou cruel.

20:57.150 --> 21:00.110
Wert thou to console me against thy meager bosom,

21:00.110 --> 21:02.120
I would forgive and forget this dark past!

21:02.990 --> 21:06.410
Brutes! Thou wouldst confine me in the dark ground once again!?

21:06.410 --> 21:09.660
I am BUER, the demon king, the philosopher of hell!

21:09.660 --> 21:11.630
So that's BUER, I take it?

21:11.630 --> 21:14.880
Indeed, voice that hints of a bosom most small.

21:14.880 --> 21:16.880
I am endowed with five legs of the go—

21:16.880 --> 21:18.970
Are you still unfinished?

21:19.880 --> 21:22.430
Nay! BUER is complete!

21:22.430 --> 21:27.350
I am the Central Nervous Unit—the key to BUER,
equipped with cipher intelligence!

21:27.350 --> 21:30.890
Tis no exaggeration to say I am its spirit!

21:30.890 --> 21:36.530
Mine giant willful body be currently at rest,
yet starting up in normal fashion!

21:37.730 --> 21:40.450
<i>So, my old friend Uzal...</i>

21:40.450 --> 21:42.660
<i>You finished it after all!?</i>

21:42.660 --> 21:45.950
<i>The terrorist attack on the city, Uzal's puppet showing up...</i>

21:45.950 --> 21:47.700
<i>It's all connected!</i>

21:48.290 --> 21:50.000
<i>I've been left with quite a handful.</i>

21:50.000 --> 21:52.620
<i>I won't let this thing slip from my grasp, not for Uzal or anybody else.</i>

21:52.620 --> 21:55.420
<i>Now that it's been pushed off on me, it's all mine!</i>

21:55.420 --> 21:57.840
Come home before it gets late, you two.

21:57.840 --> 21:58.960
Yes, ma'am.

21:59.920 --> 22:01.930
Excuse me, about the rest of my group...

22:03.430 --> 22:06.350
You obtained the key by the designated time.

22:06.350 --> 22:08.060
I'll call off the executions.

22:09.060 --> 22:11.480
Now nothing stands in the way of stealing BUER!

22:11.480 --> 22:13.730
"Stealing" makes this sound so scandalous.

22:13.730 --> 22:15.650
Now that Sahar Schehera is dead,

22:16.570 --> 22:19.730
that thing... belongs to me.

22:41.090 --> 22:44.090
Accessing the device named nature

22:44.090 --> 22:47.100
The circuit of infinite synapses

22:49.470 --> 22:52.850
Exchanging loops causes inevitable encounters

22:53.270 --> 22:56.020
What's with you and not wanting your ears touched, Clarin?

22:53.560 --> 23:04.150
{talk}{this is pandoradio, it'll change each week, ignore this segemnt}

22:56.020 --> 22:56.940
Are they sensitive?

22:56.940 --> 22:58.520
That's classified information.

22:58.520 --> 23:00.440
You're adorable when you refuse!

23:00.440 --> 23:02.070
Maybe I wanna touch them after all!

23:02.070 --> 23:04.070
Don't make that mistake.

23:04.150 --> 23:05.530
Saving data

23:05.530 --> 23:06.910
Strengthening predictions

23:06.910 --> 23:09.910
Even my latest updates

23:09.910 --> 23:15.210
can't help explain why you're so nice to me

23:15.210 --> 23:16.790
error error

23:16.790 --> 23:18.290
parameter

23:18.290 --> 23:21.630
Please help me understand

23:21.630 --> 23:23.800
where these emotions came from

23:23.800 --> 23:27.010
Find me at the end of this digital maze

23:27.010 --> 23:29.760
of feelings I can no longer control

23:29.760 --> 23:31.770
I understand the concept of emotions

23:31.770 --> 23:35.140
but I can't make any sense of my own

23:35.520 --> 23:38.150
I want to pull out these cords

23:38.480 --> 23:40.900
and head straight to you

23:40.900 --> 23:43.320
I won't come to understand love

23:43.320 --> 23:47.070
without having you here with me

23:52.290 --> 23:54.660
Nene, you're going to attend an online school!

23:54.660 --> 23:57.870
But wouldn't you rather me get a job to repay you?

23:57.870 --> 24:01.460
A child's job is to study.

24:01.460 --> 24:02.210
Yes, ma'am...

24:02.210 --> 24:04.130
Meanwhile, I'll help myself to BUER...
